  "result": "Fixed. Shell completion now keeps `#` inside arguments instead of truncating them.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex` with `whitespace_split=True`, but `shlex` still treats `#` as a comment start by default. So `cmd foo#bar baz` was parsed as `['cmd', 'foo']`, and `cmd #x y` as `['cmd']`. Every shell's completer goes through this function, so the bad parse affected bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell alike.\n\n**Change:**\n- `src/click/shell_completion.py`: set `lex.commenters = \"\"` in `split_arg_string`, with a comment explaining why.\n- `tests/test_shell_completion.py`: added `test_split_arg_string_hash`, which covers `a#b`, a leading `#`, a trailing `#`, and quoted `#` values.\n\n**Verification:** I reproduced the bug against the source tree before the change (importing from `src`, not an installed copy). After the change, `tests/test_shell_completion.py` passes (62 tests) and the full suite passes (1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry or commit anything. Let me know if you want either.",
